      <h2 class="reveal">What the data buyer looks for</h2>
      <p class="reveal">These are the published minimums. The company also has to own the records in those systems.</p>
      <div class="criteria-strip reveal">
        <div class="criteria-item"><strong>30+</strong><span>full-time U.S. office staff, or 10+ for accounting, finance and medical firms, 6+ for law firms</span></div>
        <div class="criteria-item"><strong>3+</strong><span>years of operating history, with those years of records still in the company&rsquo;s systems</span></div>
        <div class="criteria-item"><strong>5+</strong><span>systems holding the work, such as email, chat, file storage and CRM</span></div>
        <div class="criteria-item"><strong>Half</strong><span>of the staff or more working from U.S. offices</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
